    "stem": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Sexual reproduction in plants and animals involves:",
        "source": {
          "qp": 8
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "items": [
          "the formation of gametes as a result of meiosis",
          "the process of fertilisation."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "parts": [
      {
        "key": "a",
        "label": "(a)",
        "source": {
          "qp": 8,
          "ms": 13
        },
        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In most species of plants and animals, the cell that is formed as a result of fertilisation is diploid and contains homologous chromosomes.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 8
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Explain why the cell that is formed as a result of fertilisation is a diploid cell <b>and</b> contains homologous chromosomes.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "marks": 3,
        "topics": [
          {
            "ref": "16.1(2)",
            "role": "primary"
          },
          {
            "ref": "16.1(1)",
            "role": "secondary"
          }
        ],
        "markScheme": {
          "marks": 3,
          "instruction": "<i>any </i><b><i>three</i></b><i> from: </i> <i> </i>",
          "guidance": [],
          "points": [
            {
              "n": 1,
              "text": "1  (diploid) cell formed from (two) haploid gametes <b>; </b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 2,
              "text": "2  (diploid) cell has two sets of chromosomes / one set of chromosomes from each gamete <b>;</b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 3,
              "text": "3  (homologous chromosomes) maternal and paternal chromosomes<b> ;</b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 4,
              "text": "4  (homologous chromosomes) has same, genes / loci / banding pattern / centromere position / size / length <b>;</b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "er": [],
        "aiSupplement": {
          "explanation": [
            {
              "text": "Homologous chromosomes carry the same gene loci but can carry different alleles. Each homologue comes from a different parent.",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:16.1(2)",
                "ms:a#1"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reasoningChain": [
            "Identify matching chromosomes as a pair.",
            "Distinguish shared loci from identical alleles."
          ],
          "inferredMistakes": [
            {
              "text": "Saying that homologous chromosomes must contain identical alleles",
              "basis": "inferred",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:16.1(2)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "type": "short"
      },
      {
        "key": "b",
        "label": "(b)",
        "source": {
          "qp": 8,
          "ms": 13
        },
        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "State the name of the stage in meiosis when reduction division occurs <b>and</b> explain a reason for your choice.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 8
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "answerLines",
            "labels": [
              "stage in meiosis",
              "reason"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "marks": 2,
        "topics": [
          {
            "ref": "16.1(3)",
            "role": "primary"
          }
        ],
        "markScheme": {
          "marks": 2,
          "instruction": null,
          "guidance": [],
          "points": [
            {
              "n": 1,
              "text": "anaphase 1 / telophase 1 <b>;  </b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 2,
              "text": "separation of, homologous chromosomes / bivalent <b>;</b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "er": [],
        "aiSupplement": {
          "explanation": [
            {
              "text": "Reduction in meiosis I separates homologous chromosomes, so fertilisation can restore diploidy without doubling chromosome sets each generation.",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:16.1(3)",
                "ms:b#1"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reasoningChain": [
            "Identify the division that separates homologues.",
            "Link haploid gametes to restoration of diploidy at fertilisation."
          ],
          "inferredMistakes": [
            {
              "text": "Locating the reduction in chromosome sets in meiosis II",
              "basis": "inferred",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:16.1(3)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "type": "short"
      },
      {
        "key": "c",
        "label": "(c)",
        "source": {
          "qp": 9
        },
        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Microscope slides can be prepared for viewing with a light microscope to show the different stages of meiosis in plant cells.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 9
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In the male reproductive organ of plants, meiosis takes place in cells known as pollen mother cells.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 9
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fig. 4.1 and Fig. 4.2 show photomicrographs of two different stages of meiosis in pollen mother cells from a lily plant, <i>Lilium</i>.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 9
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "figure",
            "id": "fig4.1",
            "caption": "Fig. 4.1",
            "src": "figures/q4_fig4_1.png",
            "alt": "Meiosis in a lily",
            "source": {
              "qp": 9
            }
          },
          {
